    "result": "I implemented `parse_line` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. I haven't run it or any tests, since shell access wasn't available.\n\nIt checks the argument types and the separator, then scans the line one field at a time:\n- **Quoted fields:** a field starting with `\"` ends at the next `\"` that isn't doubled, and `\"\"` becomes one `\"`. The separator, `\\r` and `\\n` are ordinary characters inside quotes.\n- **Unquoted fields:** these keep their whitespace and run up to the next separator.\n- **Separator count:** a trailing separator gives a final empty field, so `\"a,\"` gives `[\"a\", \"\"]`.\n\nIt raises `ValueError` for an unterminated quote, any character other than the separator right after a closing quote, a `\"` inside an unquoted field, and a `\\r` or `\\n` outside quotes.",
